412 - Cover With His Life
 / 
Key: Db
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 412
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[Db]Look upon Jesus, sinless is He; Father, impute His life unto me.
[Db]My life of [Ab]scarlet, my sin and [Db]woe, Cover with His life, whiter than snow.
[Gb]Cover with His life, whiter [Db]than snow; [Ab7]Fullness of [Db]His [Ab7]life then [Db]shall I know;
[Gb]My life of scarlet, my [Db]sin [Ebm]and woe, Cover with His life, whiter than [Ab]snow.

Refrain:
[Ab]Cover [Db]with His life, whiter than snow;
[Gb]Fullness of His life then shall I know;
[Gb/Db]My life of scarlet, [Db]my sin and woe,
[Ab7]Cover with His life, [Db]whither than snow.

Verse 2:
[Db]Deep are the wounds transgression has made;
[Db]Red are [Ab]the stains; [Db]my soul is afraid.
[Gb]O to be covered, [Ab7]Jesus, with [Db]Thee,
[Gb]Safe from the [Db]law [Ebm]that now judgeth me!

Verse 3:
[Db]Longing the joy of pardon to know;
[Db]Jesus [Ab]holds out [Db]a robe white as snow;
[Gb]"Lord, I accept [Db/Ab]it! [Ab7]Leaving my [Db]own,
[Gb]Gladly I [Db]wear [Ebm]Thy pure life alone."

Verse 4:
[Db]Reconciled by His death for my sin,
[Db]Justified [Ab]by His [Db]life pure and clean,
[Gb]Sanctified by [Db]obeying [Ab7]His [Db]word,
[Gb]Glorified when [Ebm]returneth my Lord.
